WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.031
Levi Strauss was born Löb Strauß in Bavaria in 1829

2
00:00:05.031 --> 00:00:09.855
and came to the United States as a teenager in 1847.

3
00:00:10.205 --> 00:00:13.621
In New York he joined the dry-goods business run by his older brothers

4
00:00:13.621 --> 00:00:17.183
and learned the trade of importing and selling cloth and household goods.

5
00:00:17.533 --> 00:00:21.294
He became a United States citizen in 1853.

6
00:00:21.644 --> 00:00:26.906
He built a dry-goods business in gold-rush San Francisco, and in 1873 he

7
00:00:26.906 --> 00:00:32.534
and the tailor Jacob Davis patented the riveted work trouser — the blue jean.

8
00:00:32.884 --> 00:00:37.296
The blue jean was a joint invention: the rivet idea was Jacob Davis's.

9
00:00:37.646 --> 00:00:39.978
Strauss was the partner who financed and

10
00:00:39.978 --> 00:00:43.184
manufactured it, not the lone genius of popular legend.

11
00:00:43.534 --> 00:00:47.121
An immigrant's name became a word spoken in every country on earth.

12
00:00:47.471 --> 00:00:50.374
Read the full story, with every source, on this page.
